.TH "ODS2CASCADE" "1" "Jan 20, 2026" "0.1.0-alpha1" "Ods2Cascade"
.SH NAME
ods2cascade \- Ods2Cascade CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.sp
\fBods2cascade\fP \fB[\-h|\-\-help|\-V|\-\-version]\fP \fB<path/to/casade.toml>\fP \fB<path/to/opendnssec/conf.xml>\fP \fB<path/to/write/files/to>\fP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.sp
\fBods2cascade\fP is a command line tool to assist with migration from OpenDNSSEC to cascade\&.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \(ga\(ga<path/to/cascade.toml>\(ga\(ga
The path to the configuration file of the Cascade instance that you wish
to migrate to.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \(ga\(ga<path/to/opendnssec/conf.xml>\(ga\(ga
The path to the configuration file of the OpenDNSSEC instance that you wish
to migrate from.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \(ga\(ga<path/to/write/files/to>\(ga\(ga
The path to a directory to be created which will contain generated
documentation, scripts and  configuration files for use when migrating and
will be tailored to your specific OpenDNSSEC instance.
.UNINDENT
.SH SEE ALSO
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \X'tty: link https://cascade.docs.nlnetlabs.nl'\fI\%https://cascade.docs.nlnetlabs.nl\fP\X'tty: link'
Cascade online documentation.
.UNINDENT
